Short:        Own cloud storage client for AmigaOS 3
Author:       Ronny Krueger
Uploader:     Ronny Krueger
Type:         comm/net
Version:      @VERSION@
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.0.0
Requires:     TCP/IP stack (bsdsocket.library), AmiSSL 5, MUI 3.8 (commander)
Distribution: Aminet
Replaces:     comm/net/AmiCloud.lha

AmiCloud connects your Amiga to your own AmiCloud server over HTTPS.
Files can be used from the command line (amicloud), an interactive shell
(amicloud-shell), a two-pane MUI file manager (amicloud-commander), a
folder sync tool (amicloud-sync) or simply as the DOS volume AMICLOUD:
provided by a filesystem handler. AmiCloudPrefs edits the settings.

The server (PHP 7.4+, MariaDB) and the same tools for macOS, Linux and
Windows are part of the source distribution.

Installation
------------
Unpack the archive and double-click "Install-AmiCloud" (Commodore
Installer, part of OS 3.2 in SYS:System). Without the Installer, use the
shell script instead:  CD AmiCloud  and  Execute Install-AmiCloud.shell
Existing settings and an existing DOSDriver are never overwritten.

Requirements
------------
- AmigaOS 3.x, 68000 or better, no FPU needed
- a TCP/IP stack with bsdsocket.library (Roadshow, AmiTCP, Miami, ...)
- AmiSSL 5
- MUI 3.8 or newer for amicloud-commander only
- an AmiCloud server (see docs/INSTALL.md in the sources)

Documentation and user interface are in German.
Die Dokumentation (Docs/AmiCloud.guide) und die Programme sind deutsch.

